      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=25,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[4-\\frac{1}{5}X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-\\frac{1}{5}$ and $b=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[4-\\frac{1}{5}X] & ={(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\cdot 25 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
